>> title: Chikuzenni
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: japanese, chicken, root vegetables, dashi, simmered, make ahead, new year
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: 筑前煮, chikuzenni, chikuzenni, ちくぜんに, 煮しめ, nishime, gameni, がめ煮, simmered chicken and root vegetables
>> pairs-with: dashi, gohan
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: forgiving — cooked properly dry it keeps four days and is meant to be eaten cold out of the fridge, which is why it is made three days before New Year; left wet it keeps two and turns first at the konnyaku, which goes sour before anything looks wrong
>> step.1: The one 煮物 that is fried before it is simmered, and then simmered until it is dry again. Vegetable ratio: dashi 10 : soy 1 : mirin 1 : sake 1.
>> step.2: soak 20 min
>> step.3: fry 6 min in sesame oil
>> step.4: drop lid, simmer 20 min
>> step.5: uncover, cook dry
>> step.6: scatter over

The one 煮物 that is fried before it is simmered and then simmered until it is dry again. That is what makes it keep, and what makes it a Sunday batch as much as a New Year dish. The ratio is the vegetable one: dashi 10 : soy 1 : mirin 1 : sake 1.

Soak @dried shiitake{6} in @warm water{1%cup}(240 mL) ~soak{20%min}, until the caps are floppy through the stem. Squeeze them out over the bowl and slice them; the water stays, because it is half the seasoning.

Fry @chicken thighs{1%lb}(450 g; boneless, in 1 1/2-inch pieces), @burdock root{4%oz}(115 g; shaved and soaked 5 min), @lotus root{5%oz}(150 g; in 1/4-inch half-moons), @carrot{1}(rolled-cut into wedges) and @konnyaku{5%oz}(150 g; torn into pieces) in @toasted sesame oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #heavy pot{} ~fry{6%min}, until the chicken has gone white outside and every vegetable face is glossy.

Pour @dashi{2%cups}(475 mL), @soy sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @mirin{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @sake{3%Tbs}(45 mL) and @sugar{1%Tbs} over @&(~1)fried chicken and roots{} with @&(2)soaked shiitake and their water{}, lay a drop lid on and ~simmer{20%min}.

Lift the drop lid off @&(~1)pot{} and ~reduce{10%min}, shaking it rather than stirring, until there is a spoonful of syrupy liquid left and everything has taken a shine.

Scatter @snow peas{12}(blanched 1 min, halved on the bias) over @&(~1)chikuzenni{}, off the heat, so they stay green in the box all week.
